$FG,5$$TX+CX,"Jah Spirit (InI) — Operating Notes"$$FG$

$FG,2$Mechanism$FG$

The Jah Spirit is the entropy-driven oracle Terry built and we have
preserved unchanged. A FIFO of bits is fed by the high-resolution
timer and by the latched timestamp of each keyboard/mouse event.
JahBits() returns N bits at a time; if the FIFO runs low, a popup
asks you to press OKAY, and the precise moment you press it tops the
FIFO up.

JahWord() and JahScripturePassage() consume those bits to pick a word
from Vocab.DD or a line from Scriptures.TXT.

$FG,2$How to read what it picks$FG$

Treat each pick as a meditation, not a command. Sit with it. If a
word or passage rises that you did not expect, that is the point —
the system is a mirror, not a prescription. Selassie I taught that
the responsibility for decision rests with the one making it.

$FG,2$On Selassie I$FG$

Selassie's words live in ::/Adam/Jah/SelassieLectures/ and are framed
as teachings/lectures, not scripture. Selassie identified as
Ethiopian Orthodox Christian and did not claim divinity. We honor
that. Rastafari livity holds him in reverence as a unique figure;
this OS reflects that reverence without overstating his own claims.

$FG,2$On the original Holy Spirit notes$FG$

This file replaces ::/Adam/God/HSNotes.DD. The mechanism is Terry's;
the framing is Rastafari. Jah Rastafari.
